From f2412fa5b1fd7f2d734d10ab547089e6f4ed79e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: orangpt <orangpthub@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:25:36 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] xray: run one Xray outbound in an embedded xray-core
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds an outbound type "xray" whose options carry a complete Xray outbound
object. It is loaded into an embedded xray-core and sing-box dials through
it (core.Dial / core.DialUDP), so transports sing-box lacks — XHTTP above
all, which Russian whitelist-bypass servers depend on — work with exactly
the settings a subscription ships. xray-core's system dialer is pointed at
a sing-box dialer so its sockets follow sing-box's interface binding (and
Android's protect) instead of looping into our own TUN.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
